audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: Who owns the document type contract, and why is the structure check written in POSIX sh?

Records that docs-gov owns the document type contract in packages/docs-gov/document-types.yaml, projects only assign types to paths, and `engsys docs check` stays POSIX sh.
Translated from Korean to English; frontmatter, keys (`assign`, `exempt`, `deferred`, `frozen-status`, `pattern`), paths and the ADR 0001/0004/0005 and design 0002 links are unchanged.
Original section order (Decision, Background, Rationale and Alternatives, Consequences) is kept; frozen records are checked for section presence only.
유예 rendered as deferred/deferral, 배정 as assign, 안내 as guidance, per the glossary.
The statement about the two deferred docs/design documents is kept as a historical fact, not updated to today's state. No Korean literals retained.

